🫀 GeoSentinel-DCM
A Geometric Deep Learning and Multimodal Multiscale Digital Twin Framework for Precision Risk Stratification in Dilated Cardiomyopathy
Python 3.10+PyTorch Geometric 
License: MIT
 
Status: Code & Manuscript Ready
 
Platform: Linux / Windows


📖 Overview
GeoSentinel-DCM is an end-to-end, multi-tier geometric deep learning and digital twin framework designed for clinical risk stratification and survival prognosis in Dilated Cardiomyopathy (DCM).

🚀 Installation & Quickstart
1. Clone Repository & Setup Environment
bash

# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/YourUsername/GeoSentinel-DCM.git
cd GeoSentinel-DCM
# Create Conda Environment
conda create -n geosentinel python=3.10 -y
conda activate geosentinel
# Install PyTorch & PyTorch Geometric (adjust CUDA version as needed)
pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118
pip install torch-geometric torch-scatter torch-sparse -f https://data.pyg.org/whl/torch-2.1.0+cu118.html
# Install Clinical Survival & Image Processing Packages
pip install lifelines scikit-survival nibabel pyvista trimesh shap scikit-learn pandas numpy matplotlib
2. End-to-End Inference & Risk Prediction
To run the complete 4-Pillar inference and SAR Fusion Engine on patient data:

bash

# Execute SAR Fusion Pipeline
python src/ml/final_submission_v26_prognosis.py \
    --input_dir Dataset/ \
    --output_dir output/ \
    --endpoint primary

